hl.lore.ambience=§lSounds§r\n\nFootsteps behind you, doors, chests, distant mining, the hiss of a creeper that isn't there, breathing, nails on the wall, knocking, your name whispered.\n\n§eTip:§r don't turn around. Or do.
hl.lore.gamer=§lHerobrineGamer788§r\n§8(a player who shouldn't be here)§r\n\nHe joins your world like anyone else, wearing a headset whose red light never blinks. He plays, copies you, turns strange and in the end stops pretending.\n\n§eTip:§r when he reveals himself, look on the ground where he stood.
hl.lore.dweller=§lThe Cave Dweller§r\n§8(inspired by Cave Dweller / From The Caves)§r\n\nA pale, eyeless body on four very long limbs, knees above its back. Its four-lipped snout opens like a flower over rings of teeth. It flees if you catch it looking; wait too long and it comes for you.\n\n§eTip:§r the flashlight drives it off. Live through it and it leaves something behind.
hl.lore.mimic=§lThe Mimic§r\n§8(the chest that bites)§r\n\nA chest just like yours, where there was nothing before. Open it and the lid is a mouth full of teeth, and six legs unfold.\n\n§eTip:§r it can be killed, and drops what it swallowed: iron, gold, emeralds... sometimes a diamond.
hl.lore.statue=§lThe Weeping Statue§r\n§8(inspired by the Weeping Angels and SCP-173)§r\n\nA stone figure with its face in its hands. It doesn't move while anyone is looking. Every time you look away, or blink, it's closer, its hands lower, its mouth wider.\n\n§eTip:§r keep your eyes on it until it gives up. A Ward Lantern stops it.
hl.lore.herobrine=§lHerobrine§r\n§8(the old legend)§r\n\nThree blocks tall, his stomach open and stitched, his ribs splayed like fingers, half his face burned to the bone, his jaw hanging to his chest. His spine comes out of his back and arches over his head like a scorpion's tail. He watches from afar and vanishes if you look.\n\n§eTip:§r stare him down three times. Don't hit him.
hl.lore.goatman=§lThe Goatman§r\n§8(the legend of the woods)§r\n\nGoat legs, ram's horns, yellow eyes, arms too human. He screams like a goat between the trees at night. He comes closer when you don't look; when you catch him he screams and runs... or comes for you.\n\n§eTip:§r light and a beating send him running.
hl.lore.fog=§lThe Man From The Fog§r\n§8(inspired by The Man From The Fog)§r\n\nOver three blocks of grey, starved body in a soaked black raincoat. Inside the hood, two white points and a grin from ear to ear. He comes closer when you don't look. At night he knocks on your door.\n\n§eTip:§r live through a fog in which you saw him.
hl.lore.skinwalker=§lThe Skinwalker§r\n§8(the desert legend)§r\n\nA cow that is always looking at you, with a person's eyes and a person's teeth. You hear your name in the field, someone hurt where nobody is. Get close and it stands up: a starved thing with the cow's skull for a face and its hide on its back.\n\n§eTip:§r don't go near cows that stare. Hurt, it flees.
hl.lore.shadow=§lThe Shadow§r\n§8(the Hat Man)§r\n\nA flat black figure in a wide-brimmed hat and a coat that frays into smoke. It puts out the lights in your house, follows you, looks in through the window, and stands at the foot of your bed when you wake.\n\n§eTip:§r the flashlight, or staring at it, makes it vanish. A Ward Lantern keeps it out.
hl.lore.drowned=§lThe Drowned One§r\n§8(what never came out of the water)§r\n\nSwollen, in a torn green nightdress, black hair over its face but for one eye. It gurgles under the surface. At night it watches from the shallows; if you swim, it grabs you from below and pulls.\n\n§eTip:§r hit it to make it let go, or get out of the water.
hl.lore.null=§lnull§r\n§8(inspired by The Broken Script)§r\n\nA player the game can't draw: black, torn into slices that don't line up, fringed red and blue, two white eyes and the F3+B box round it. It writes in the chat, corrupts blocks, pretends the game has frozen.\n\n§eTip:§r look it in the eye. Twice.
hl.lore.e303=§lEntity 303§r\n§8(the hacker who never left)§r\n\nWhite hood, red eyes, a mask with a stitched grin. He joins your game, writes in the chat, swaps what you're holding, kicks you (or pretends to). In person he floats, raises his hands and your world is his: you fly, you're teleported, lightning falls. Then he bans you.\n\n§eTip:§r sit through his show. In the end he leaves something.
hl.lore.siren=§lSiren Head§r\n§8(inspired by Trevor Henderson's creature)§r\n\nNearly six blocks of dried skin over bones, and where the head should be, a pole with two rusted loudspeakers. First you hear the siren, far away. Then voices through the speakers. Watch it too long and it comes, in huge strides.\n\n§eTip:§r hide where it can't see you (under a roof, behind a hill) until it loses you.
hl.lore.wendigo=§lThe Wendigo§r\n§8(hunger that learned to walk)§r\n\nBlue-white skin over its ribs, fingers black with frostbite, a deer's skull with huge antlers. It whistles between the trees. It hunts by sound: run and it hears you; crouch and keep still and it loses you. Its claws leave you starving.\n\n§eTip:§r in the snow, crouch.
hl.lore.redNight=§lThe Red Night§r\n\nEvery four days, a night of red fog when everything comes twice as often and your lanterns may go out. It ends at dawn.
hl.lore.boss=§l§4The Hollow Miner§r\n§8(Herobrine, in his true form)§r\n\nNearly five blocks of cracked deepslate with lava inside, his miner's helmet with the lamp still lit, a pickaxe for a right hand, a fist of stone, and his spine arching over his head to an obsidian sting. He teleports, calls down lightning, summons Dwellers, puts out the light and stings. At half health he flies into a rage.\n\n§eTip:§r flashlight light burns him.
hl.page.1.title=I. The Player
hl.page.1.text=§oDay 3. A player joined my world. His name was HerobrineGamer788. He wore a headset with a red light. He gave me bread.\n\nDay 4. Today he copied my every step. Every block I mined, he mined.\n\nDay 5. The light on his headset doesn't blink. Neither does he.
hl.page.2.title=II. What Lives Below
hl.page.2.text=§oThere's something in the mine that copies my footsteps. It has no eyes. It doesn't need them.\n\nWhen it opens its mouth, its whole face opens.\n\nIt hates light. I'm running out of batteries.
hl.page.3.title=III. White Eyes
hl.page.3.text=§oI found his pickaxe buried in his own shoulder. He was a miner. He dug too deep, where the stone breathes, and something came back up with him.\n\nNow his eyes are white and his spine is outside his body, raised over his head like a scorpion's tail.
hl.page.4.title=IV. The Fog
hl.page.4.text=§oThe fog isn't fog. It's him, waiting, hood up, with that grin.\n\nIf you look at him, he leaves. If you don't, he comes closer.\n\nHe knocked on my door three times. The fourth time he didn't knock.
hl.page.5.title=V. The Error
hl.page.5.text=§oBlocks break into magenta and black. The world comes apart where he walks.\n\nThere's another one. He says he's an admin. He bans me every night and every morning I'm still here.
hl.page.6.title=VI. The Siren
hl.page.6.text=§oThe siren wails at night, always far away. I saw it once: taller than the pines, perfectly still, two loudspeakers where its head should be.\n\nI looked at it too long. I hid in a cave and waited until I couldn't hear it any more.\n\nThrough the speakers it was saying my name.
hl.page.7.title=VII. The Name
hl.page.7.text=§oThey all serve him. The one in the mine, the one with the tail of bone.\n\nIf you gather these seven pages, call him by his name at night, under the sky. He will come in his true form, and only then can he be hurt.\n\nI can't any more. I don't think I'm the one playing now.
hl.threat.scares=Scares
hl.lore.scares=§lScares§r\n\nNot a creature: the moments when something is too close. A face right in front of yours for the length of a blink. Breath on the back of your neck and something brushing past. A door slamming in an empty house. The screen tearing into static. A blow that hurts and leaves no mark. Your name, written across your eyes.
hl.arrive.scares=§8[???]§r §7Don't blink. Don't turn round. Don't look behind the door.
hl.scare.neck=§7§oSomething brushed the back of your neck.
hl.scare.name_sub=§8i'm watching you
hl.threat.phobias=The Fears
hl.lore.phobias=§lThe Fears§r\n\nEveryone is afraid of something, and the game knows what. Stand in the dark with no light, on a ledge very high up, in very deep water, or in a tunnel you barely fit in, and a fear slowly fills. When it is full, something made exactly for it happens. And it is loud.\n\n§eTip:§r carry a light, don't look down, get out of the water and stay out of narrow tunnels. The journal shows how full each fear is.
hl.arrive.phobias=§8[???]§r §7We know what you're afraid of.
