hl.lore.rake=§lThe Rake§r\n§8(inspired by The Rake creepypasta)§r\n\nSomething pale and hairless, the size of a man, that never stands like one. It crouches in fields with its knees by its ears and its arms hanging to the ground, watching you with two huge black eyes. While you look it doesn't move; look too long and it shrieks and runs off on all fours. Look away and it is closer. Some nights, when you wake up, it is at the foot of your bed.\n\n§eTip:§r keep your eyes on it, but don't go near. The flashlight drives it off.
hl.lore.echo=§lThe Echo§r\n\nWhat lives in the Ancient City. Nearly three blocks of something that was a person once, grown through with sculk, its chest open and a heart beating cyan inside. It has no eyes: it hears. Your footsteps, the blocks you break, the doors. Make too much noise and it comes for you, and it hits harder than anything down there. It copies what it has heard, to bring you closer.\n\n§eTip:§r crouch and keep still: it loses you. It never leaves the city.
hl.lore.steps=§lFootsteps§r\n\nSomeone walks behind you, step for step. When you walk, they walk; when you stop, they stop. But every time you stop they take one more step, a little closer. Turn round and there is nobody.
hl.lore.eyes=§lThe Eyes§r\n\nIn the dark of a cave, eyes open all around you, low down between the rocks. They blink. They watch. Stare at a pair and it closes; shine a light and they all close. When the last pair closes, one more opens, right behind you.
hl.lore.countdown=§lThe Countdown§r\n\nA message from nobody: "When it reaches zero, turn around." Then the numbers, one a second. At zero the screen goes black, and when it comes back there is a face in front of yours. Or sometimes nothing... and a minute later, a scream.
hl.lore.grave=§lYour Grave§r\n\nAt night, a bell behind you. Go and look: a mound of freshly dug earth, a headstone, a black rose, and on the stone your name and tomorrow's date. Come close and something knocks. From underneath.
hl.lore.hour=§lThe Dead Hour§r\n\nThree in the morning. Every animal and villager around you stops where it is and turns to look at you, all at once, while a bell nobody owns tolls three times. Then they carry on as if nothing happened. And far away, someone screams.
hl.arrive.rake=§8[???]§r §7If you see something crouching in a field, don't go near. Don't stop looking at it.
hl.arrive.echo=§8[???]§r §7Under the deepslate there is a city. Something still lives there. It listens.
hl.arrive.steps=§8[???]§r §7When you stop, do they stop with you?
hl.arrive.eyes=§8[???]§r §7Not everything that shines in a cave is ore.
hl.arrive.countdown=§8[???]§r §710, 9, 8...
hl.arrive.grave=§8[???]§r §7Someone is digging. It's your size.
hl.arrive.hour=§8[???]§r §7At three o'clock, everything looks at you.
hl.rake.bed=§7§oThere is something at the foot of your bed.
hl.echo.near=§3§oSomething is listening. Don't make a sound.
hl.echo.heard=§3§lIt heard you.
hl.echo.lost=§3§oIt lost you. Don't move.
hl.ancient.title=§3The Ancient City
hl.ancient.sub=§8Down here, nobody makes a sound.
hl.ancient.candles=§7§oThe candles go out by themselves.
hl.ancient.steps=§7§oYour footsteps come back, a little late.
hl.ancient.portal=§5§oThe frame hums. Something is trying to come through.
hl.ancient.whisper.1=§3§oPeople lived here. Now it only listens.
hl.ancient.whisper.2=§3§oDon't run.
hl.ancient.whisper.3=§3§oWe kept quiet too long.
hl.ancient.whisper.4=§3§oIt can hear you breathing.
hl.ancient.whisper.5=§3§oThe door was not for leaving.
hl.ancient.whisper.6=§3§oStay. Like us.
hl.steps.end=§7§oSomeone breathes on your neck.
hl.countdown.start=§7When it reaches zero, turn around.
hl.countdown.nothing=§8...not yet.
